<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Bar appearance for API 29 and later.

  `android:enforceNavigationBarContrast` was introduced in API 29. It belongs in
  a versioned resource for the same reason as its API 27 sibling in
  values-v27/: the default theme is read on API 23, where lint's NewApi check
  rejects the attribute.

  Setting it false is necessary but was not sufficient on MIUI. Measured on a
  Redmi Note 12 Pro running Android 16: with the dark-only theme in place the
  status bar came out RGB(18,18,18) over 93% of its area, and the navigation bar
  stayed RGB(208,208,208) over 98%, which is the system scrim and not the theme colour.
  MainActivity therefore also calls
  `window.isNavigationBarContrastEnforced = false` for API 30+, and after both
  were in place the navigation bar measured RGB(18,18,18) like the status bar.

  Both are asserted on hardware. Neither is inferred from documentation alone.

  The parent is Theme.OcuBea.Base for the same reason as in values-v27/: a
  versioned resource replaces the default style rather than merging with it, so
  a Material parent here dropped windowBackground, the bar colours and the primary
  colour from every device running API 29 or later, which is all of them.
-->
<resources>
    <style name="Theme.OcuBea" parent="Theme.OcuBea.Base">
        <item name="android:enforceNavigationBarContrast">false</item>
    </style>
</resources>